GREP - filter lines matching a pattern
Usage: grep [-i] [-v] [-n] <pattern> [file...]

Prints lines that contain the pattern. With no file, reads piped
input.

Options:
  -i  ignore case
  -v  invert the match
  -n  number the output lines

Examples:
  grep hello notes.txt
  cat log.txt | grep -i error
  ls /etc | grep man

Notes:
- The pattern matches literally; use it in pipes freely.
